1
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:13,840
Do you want a friend whom you could tell everything to, like your deepest feelings and thoughts?

2
00:00:14,580 --> 00:00:19,580
Or are you afraid that your friend would laugh at you, or would not understand what you're

3
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:20,600
going through?

4
00:00:21,740 --> 00:00:24,160
Anne Frank wanted the first kind,

5
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:27,020
so she made her diary her best friend.

6
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:33,000
Anne lived in Amsterdam in the Netherlands during World War II.

7
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:51,200
During that time the only true friend was her diary.

8
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:57,880
She said, “I don’t want to set down a series of facts in a diary as most people do,

9
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:00,800
but I want this diary itself to be my friend,

10
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:05,440
and I shall call my friend Kitty.” Now read how she felt

11
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:09,300
after being in the hiding place since July 1942.

12
00:01:12,140 --> 00:01:16,800
Thursday 15, June, 1944 Dear kitty,

13
00:01:17,980 --> 00:01:21,800
I wonder if it’s because I haven’t been able to be outdoors

14
00:01:21,800 --> 00:01:25,700
for so long that I’ve grown so crazy about everything to do

15
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:26,360
with nature.

16
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:31,900
I can well remember that there was a time when a deep blue sky,

17
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:37,600
the song of the birds, moonlight and flowers could never have kept me spellbound.

18
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,920
That’s changed since I was here.

19
00:01:54,240 --> 00:01:56,900
But as the moon gave far too much light,

20
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:59,120
I didn’t dare open a window.

21
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:11,800
I didn’t go downstairs until the window had to be shut.

22
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:40,020
It’s no pleasure looking through these any longer because nature is one thing

23
00:02:40,020 --> 00:02:41,980
that really must be experienced.
